<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>The rest of the day</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>PE, every day</h3><p>Team sport, fitness, and free play. By this age most students have found their thing, and we make room for it.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Vocational classes</h3><p>Rotating specialist subjects, this year technology, fashion and design, and art. Assessed by what gets made. Older students often work alongside younger ones on shared projects.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Year 9 Checkpoint</h3><p>Optional Cambridge diagnostic in English, Maths, and Science at the end of Year 9. Useful preparation for exam-based pathways in Upper Years, and a clear report for families.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>What comes next</h3><p>After Year 9 students move into <a href="{{ '/learning/upper-years/' | url }}">Upper Years</a>, where they choose between a US diploma and a Cambridge pathway.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

